<section xml:id="aboutcsp">

  <title>About AP CSP</title>

  <p>
  AP Computer Science Principles (CSP) is an introductory college-level computing course 
  designed to introduce students to the field of computer science and its applications.
  Rather than focusing only on coding, AP CSP explores the broader ideas of computing,
  including algorithms, Artificial Intelligence (AI), data, the Internet, cybersecurity, 
  and the impacts of computing on society. No prior programming experience is required.
  Find out more about the AP exam at <url href="https://apcentral.collegeboard.org/courses/ap-computer-science-principles">
  College Board AP CSP site</url>. </p>
  
  <p>CSPossible was created to follow the currently being redesigned College Board AP CSP framework 
    and exam which will go into effect in 2028.
  </p>
 
 </section>